{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789513152,"nonce":"2xPKAX1fgJEcUR+U9zCEdgDVELE=","title":"A field assigned a conditional expression stored before the value existed","message":"`self.x = self.x if self.x \u003e other.x else other.x` with typed float fields put the store in the block the statement started in, ahead of the branch that computes the value, so the store named a phi defined later and Cranelift panicked with \"no entry found for key\". `translate_assignment` translated the value with the plain entry and kept using that block; the value of a conditional or a short-circuit is defined where its blocks join. It now takes the continuation the value left, as a `let` does, and settles it for the statement's caller.\n\nReached from Python once method parameters were typed (the arms were dynamic calls before); the same shape in any frontend was affected.","files":null}]}